  "id": "Compound::DB00220 - Gene::1565",
  "verbalization": "Nelfinavir is implicated in the regulation of Cyp2d6 through a series of interconnected molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Nelfinavir binds to Cyp3a7-cyp3a51p, which in turn is bound by Rifapentine or Praziquantel, both of which subsequently bind to Cyp2d6. This indicates that Nelfinavir may influence Cyp2d6 through a chain of interactions involving other cytochrome P450 enzymes. The lowest common ancestors of these interactions, such as Nelfinavir and Praziquantel, are classified as Anti-Infective Agents, suggesting a potential role in drug metabolism. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Nelfinavir could modulate Cyp2d6 activity, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
